WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.438
Measure protected coverage and
effectiveness, not that a setting exists.

2
00:00:04.438 --> 00:00:06.762
The guide's metrics are design guidance,

3
00:00:06.762 --> 00:00:10.213
and each divides what's protected
and tested by what exists.

4
00:00:10.213 --> 00:00:13.671
Exposure ownership: register
rows with an owner,

5
00:00:13.671 --> 00:00:16.438
over all rows, target a hundred percent.

6
00:00:16.438 --> 00:00:20.492
DDoS coverage: public I Ps with
Network or I P Protection,

7
00:00:20.492 --> 00:00:23.577
over public I Ps,
excluding NAT gateway I Ps.

8
00:00:23.577 --> 00:00:29.747
Web application firewall prevention coverage,
origin lock-down, egress inspection,

9
00:00:29.747 --> 00:00:34.859
private pass, vault posture, policy
compliance, and exemption hygiene,

10
00:00:34.859 --> 00:00:38.825
where the target is zero
exemptions past their expiry.

11
00:00:38.825 --> 00:00:39.912
Then closure.

12
00:00:39.912 --> 00:00:45.219
A finding the guide addresses is ready
for closure when every applicable control

13
00:00:45.219 --> 00:00:49.199
state, Designed, Configured,
Enforced, Evidenced and Operated,

14
00:00:49.199 --> 00:00:53.101
has evidence; the authorizing
official or assessor decides.

15
00:00:53.101 --> 00:00:57.975
Findings from a Zero Trust assessment
enter the closure chain that Zero Trust

16
00:00:57.975 --> 00:01:02.760
and Assessment sets out, weighted by
exposure and blast radius, not pass rate.
